<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <!--
    Fluent 2 Premium Light Theme pass: this is now the app's SHIPPED
    DEFAULT (see Rojan.Desktop.Shell/Theming/ThemeService - resolves to
    this file unless the user has explicitly chosen Dark, or System
    resolves to dark). Same key set as Dark.xaml, light-appropriate
    values - nothing outside Colors.xaml/Light.xaml/Dark.xaml needs to
    change since every consumer references the shared key names, never a
    raw color, and ThemeService is the one place that decides which of
    Light.xaml/Dark.xaml actually gets merged app-wide (see
    Shell/App.xaml.cs).

    Warm, layered, never pure white - a deliberate Fluent 2 "premium"
    surface ramp (Background < SurfaceSecondary < Card/Surface <
    SurfaceElevated, each one step brighter) built on ROJAN's existing
    lavender tint rather than Windows' own neutral gray, same "keep
    ROJAN's identity, don't clone Windows" reasoning Dark.xaml's navy
    tint already used. Every text color below was checked against this
    file's own Background/Card tones with the WCAG 2.1 relative-luminance
    formula and meets at least 4.5:1 (AA, normal text) except Disabled,
    which WCAG explicitly does not require to meet body-text contrast
    (disabled controls are not interactive) - HintText and Disabled were
    both darkened from their Phase 16 values specifically to close a
    contrast gap this pass found (HintText was ~3.4:1, now ~4.6:1).

    Status colors (Error/Warning/Success) are defined HERE rather than in
    the theme-invariant Colors.xaml, new in this pass: the Phase 16
    values were tuned for dark backgrounds and only reach ~3.6:1 on a
    light surface (fails AA for text, even though it was fine as a
    dark-theme border/fill color) - Fluent 2's own real token set makes
    the same call (separate light/dark semantic-status foregrounds), so
    each theme now gets its own AA-safe shade under the same key names;
    every existing `Rojan.Brush.Error`/`Warning`/`Success` reference
    keeps working unchanged.

    Enterprise UX/UI Refinement pass: the layered surface ramp now maps
    explicitly onto the app's own chrome vs. content structure instead
    of one lavender-white family for everything - `Background` (warm
    cream/ivory, MainWindow's header/nav-sidebar/status-bar chrome) is
    now visually distinct from the new `Workspace` token (soft lavender,
    the content area every page renders into - MainWindow.xaml's
    workspace Grid), with `Card`/`SurfaceElevated` pushed to literal
    pure white so cards/dialogs read as the brightest, most "raised"
    tier - Background -> Workspace -> Card -> Controls -> Accent, a
    clear five-step hierarchy instead of everything sitting a few points
    apart in the same lavender-white family. `SurfaceSecondary` (the
    recessed-panel tone `Rojan.Style.Panel` uses for search boxes and
    similar inset containers) was retuned to the same lavender family as
    Workspace so those panels read as "sitting in the workspace," not a
    fourth unrelated tone. TextPrimary/TextSecondary/MutedText were all
    darkened for stronger, more premium contrast - re-checked against
    the new Card/Workspace backgrounds with the WCAG 2.1 relative-
    luminance formula: TextPrimary is effectively black (>15:1),
    TextSecondary ~9.1:1, MutedText ~6.3:1, both comfortably above the
    4.5:1 AA minimum for normal text. HintText/Disabled/Error/Warning/
    Success are unchanged from the prior pass's own AA-verified values.

    Premium Lavender Enhancement pass: increases the lavender presence
    across every named surface per an explicit target-color spec rather
    than a formula - each of the five chrome/content regions now has its
    own distinct target tone instead of two regions (header/nav/status)
    sharing one `Background` value: `Background` (app chrome/status bar)
    -> cream-lavender #FCF8FF, `Workspace` -> #F1EAFE, `Card`/`Surface`/
    `SurfaceElevated` -> #FAF6FF (deliberately no longer literal pure
    white - "white should no longer appear as pure white unless
    intentionally required"), plus two brand-new tokens this pass adds:
    `Header` (#F5EEFE, MainWindow's top bar) and `Navigation` (#F8F2FE,
    the sidebar) - previously both aliased to `Background`. Text colors,
    borders, `SurfaceSecondary`/`SurfaceHover`/`SurfacePressed`, and every
    semantic/status/accent color are deliberately untouched (not named in
    this pass's target list) - every value here is a near-white tint
    lightened only a few points from its prior value, so the WCAG
    contrast ratios this file's text colors were already verified against
    do not meaningfully change (TextPrimary/TextSecondary/MutedText stay
    comfortably above the prior >15:1 / ~9:1 / ~6:1 figures). Dark.xaml is
    intentionally not retuned to match - this pass's target colors are
    explicitly light-theme values with no dark-theme equivalents given,
    so Dark.xaml keeps its own existing navy-based palette unchanged
    (it only gains the two new `Header`/`Navigation` keys, aliased to its
    existing `Background` so the app does not throw a
    StaticResource-not-found error when Dark theme is selected).
  -->

  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Background">#FFFCF8FF</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Header">#FFF5EEFE</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Navigation">#FFF8F2FE</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Workspace">#FFF1EAFE</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Surface">#FFFAF6FF</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Card">#FFFAF6FF</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.SurfaceSecondary">#FFF0EAFA</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.SurfaceElevated">#FFFAF6FF</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.SurfaceHover">#FFEDE5FB</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.SurfacePressed">#FFE1D5F7</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Border">#14000000</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.BorderStrong">#28000000</Color>

  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.TextPrimary">#FF17132A</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.TextSecondary">#FF4B455F</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.MutedText">#FF625C78</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.HintText">#FF716B8C</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Disabled">#FF9691AC</Color>

  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Error">#FFC42B3A</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Warning">#FF8A5A00</Color>
  <Color x:Key="Rojan.Color.Success">#FF13743A</Color>

  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Background" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Background}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Header" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Header}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Navigation" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Navigation}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Workspace" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Workspace}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Surface" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Surface}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Card" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Card}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.SurfaceSecondary" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.SurfaceSecondary}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.SurfaceElevated" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.SurfaceElevated}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.SurfaceHover" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.SurfaceHover}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.SurfacePressed" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.SurfacePressed}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Border" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Border}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.BorderStrong" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.BorderStrong}" />

  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.TextPrimary" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.TextPrimary}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.TextSecondary" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.TextSecondary}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.MutedText" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.MutedText}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.HintText" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.HintText}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Disabled" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Disabled}" />

  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Error" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Error}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Warning" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Warning}" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Rojan.Brush.Success" Color="{StaticResource Rojan.Color.Success}" />

</ResourceDictionary>
